Will people please stop messing with things in progress?

DNS updates take 12-24 hours to fully propagate — the
reason that everything works right now is that the DNS settings
for mc-stan.org <http://mc-stan.org> are using the info from 12 hours ago (i.e.
the now stale info).  Once Dan’s reversion propagates pair
will no longer direct to github correctly and we’ll be back to
square one.

And the CNAME was intentionally _not_ on the master branch.
The gh-pages branch is leftover from when the site was being
hosted as a project page all of 24 hours ago.

I’m not going to touch anything and let everything break
before I try to fix it again.  But this will take another 24 hours.
Do not touch pair or stan-dev.github.io <http://stan-dev.github.io> in this time.

